erif;font-size:13.8px;\">What we are going to listen to next is a simple experiment in which we are going to talk about train travel with an AI. Will we be able to engage in a real conversation or, on the contrary, will we be talking to a mirror or one of those talking dolls with engraved phrases?</p><p style=\"background:rgb(255,255,255);border:0px;margin:0px 0px 24px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Georgia, 'Bitstream Charter', serif;font-size:13.8px;\">We are watching the death of art take place before our eyes. If creative jobs are no longer safe from machines, even the most highly skilled jobs are in danger of becoming obsolete. What will we have left?</p>","licenseurl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/","radiaseason":"49","scanner":"Internet Archive HTML5 Uploader 1.7.0","subject":"radio art;Radia;TEA FM","title":"Show 0935: Can we talk, dear AI? by Chuse Fernandez (TEA FM)","uploader":"radia.fm@gmail.com","publicdate":"2023-02-26 19:53:40","addeddate":"2023-02-26 19:53:40","year":"2023"},"server":"ia904609.us.archive.org","uniq":904682345,"workable_servers":["ia904609.us.archive.org","ia804609.us.archive.org"]}